<!--
  BandIt Plus custom bandit cultures.

  2026-07-26 — notable_templates added to every culture.

  WHY: BanditChiefRegistry.GetOrCreateChiefClan sets IsMinorFaction = true on each
  bp_chief_clan_* clan (see that file, "Mark as non-bandit minor faction"). That flag
  routes these clans into vanilla's minor-faction hero-spawn path on the daily tick:

      CampaignEvents.DailyTickClan
        -> HeroSpawnCampaignBehavior.DailyTickClan
          -> HeroSpawnCampaignBehavior.TrySpawnHeroesAndParties
            -> HeroSpawnCampaignBehavior.SpawnMinorFactionHeroes(clan, firstTime)

  That path assumes a fully-populated culture, because in vanilla every minor faction
  (jawwal, ghilman, embers_of_flame, ...) uses one of the SIX MAIN cultures, all of
  which declare notable_templates. Vanilla BANDIT cultures (looters, sea_raiders,
  forest_bandits) declare none — but they are bandit factions, never minor factions,
  so they never reach this code.

  Our cultures were in the worst of both worlds: bandit culture data, minor-faction
  clan flag. A user running Realm of Thrones crashed on new-game character creation
  ("outlaw blood") with:

      Value cannot be null. Parameter name: source
        at System.Linq.Enumerable.Any[TSource](IEnumerable`1 source, Func`2 predicate)
        at ROT.HarmonyPatches.CustomCompanions.HeroSpawnCampaignBehaviorPatches.Prefix(Clan, Boolean)
        at HeroSpawnCampaignBehavior.SpawnMinorFactionHeroes_Patch1(Clan, Boolean)
        at HeroSpawnCampaignBehavior.TrySpawnHeroesAndParties(Clan, Boolean)

  The throwing frame belongs to another mod, but the null collection is ours: a
  culture reached by minor-faction hero spawning with no templates to enumerate.
  Vanilla tolerates the empty case; other mods LINQ over it and get null.

  Templates below are vanilla NPCCharacters from SandBoxCore (a hard dependency of
  this module, so they always resolve), mapped to the nearest vanilla culture by
  theme. This is deliberately additive: it completes the data without changing the
  IsMinorFaction/IsBanditFaction semantics the rest of the mod depends on. It also
  covers can_have_settlement="true" — a bandit-culture settlement seized by the
  Bandit King needs notable templates for the same reason.

  If a future pass wants the deeper fix, it is IsMinorFaction=false in
  BanditChiefRegistry — but note that flag interacts with encyclopedia display and
  diplomacy suppression (SiegeKingdomDiplomacySuppressPatch), and this codebase has
  already had to revert a related change (chief.IsMinorFactionHero, see the v27 note
  in BanditChiefRegistry) after it crashed the daily tick. Playtest before changing it.
-->
